{"title":"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ways can one tile the border of a triangular grid of hexagons of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> completely using\nonly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c8b62c658c4d2cde679951a8b1e450d1b88b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times  2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> hexagon tiles? Express your answer in terms of a well-known sequence, and\nprove that your answer holds true for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> (examples of such grids for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are shown below).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2369024bc980548ec3bd2535a636dde6891be97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path S=rotate(30)*polygon(6); filldraw(S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(2*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75));  filldraw(shift(6,0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(6,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75));  filldraw(shift(14,0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(4*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(7*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(14,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),6)*S,green+linewidth(.75));   filldraw(shift(24,0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(4*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3),0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(7*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(9*sqrt(3)/2,3/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(4*sqrt(3),3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); //filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(7*sqrt(3)/2,9/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(2*sqrt(3),6)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(3*sqrt(3),6)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(24,0)*shift(5*sqrt(3)/2,15/2)*S,green+linewidth(.75));  filldraw(shift(38,0)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(38,0)*shift(sqrt(3)/2,3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); filldraw(shift(38,0)*shift(-sqrt(3)/2,3)*S,green+linewidth(.75)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"62\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, consider how many ways there are to tile a line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> spaces with sets of 1 or 2. Clearly there are 1 and 2 ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202fc0afd4383c67dc485f4a9ea05f1bc682f98c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. By induction, we will show that the number of tilings is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bea4f5ee837b0249288558f2fb73a871b264491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />-th Fibonacci number (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/5953a97aea830abcad57b39e5424fc3c6b6fe51d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_1=F_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />). Suppose this is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1d97e11ace36e4a8cf46647379600b675e401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 1,2,3 ,...,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. Then for a line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe144e5517842d0ce8986c6fada40267e99bd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />, all tilings either satisfy that the first space is covered by a 1-tile or that the first space is covered by a 2-tile. If the first space is covered by a 1-tile, by our inductive hypothesis, the number of ways to tile the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> spaces is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c23685e05253ab613e009ade6563922fd1c730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{M+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />. If the first space is covered by a 2-tile, the number of ways to tile the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73ccba27a77749bc58568dd3767cfb5119fc0366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> spaces is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d178e964991ddcafb5a9aa4a23946a7de50c50d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{M}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />. Thus the total number of ways to tile the line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe144e5517842d0ce8986c6fada40267e99bd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d122cff6feed4ef336a1a725d496ab1045625dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{M+1}+F_{M} = F_{M+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nReturning to the original question, notice that the triangular border reduces to a cycle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa3ed6e2948408b3a22eb647273422a4770bed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> spaces, except for the fact that, around each of the 3 corners, there’s 2 spaces which are adjacent to three, rather than two, other spaces. We’ll separately count tilings where 0 (case 1), 1 (case 2), 2 (case 3) or 3 (case 4) of the corners have a 2-tile spanning these 2 corner-adjacent spaces.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 1: The problem reduces to a cycle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa3ed6e2948408b3a22eb647273422a4770bed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> spaces. Fix some space in the array. Any tiling of the array will satisfy that that space is a) covered by a 1-tile, b) covered by a 2-tile along with the next space counter-clockwise or c) covered by a 2-tile along with the next space clockwise. In the case of (a), once we add this 1-tile, the number of ways to tile the remaining spaces reduces to the line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf91ad448b7d4bf6d77e914b406332884b465ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. In each of (b) and (c), after adding the 2-tile the number of ways to tile the remaining spaces reduces to the line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec0748a524d0b4f3c19b07385bd845e70f93b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. This gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef7c35516785141b24b398341e999736b6b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{3n-3} + 2F_{3n-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> tiling.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 2: After the 2-tile is placed on the corner-adjacent spaces, the corner space has to be covered with a 1-tile. Then tiling the remaining spaces reduces to tiling a line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cbbde46064a599f5632f94fa546bf22f149c99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. Since there’s 3 corners, this gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd04716c5819f613ddf63b2ed3860a92d2ff33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3F_{3n-5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> tilings.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 3: After 2-tiles are placed on 2 different corner-adjacent spaces, the array is reduced to one line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cc722503ab9361e9471f3344eef06e4e2bfc7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and one line of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a1edba2319ab133dc97ef3f61b853dd756ce98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. Since there’s 3 ways to choose 2 of 3 corners, this gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea8f36f9093e5774c23bb2527e3100566410e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3F_{n-3}F_{2n-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. (Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb2fd23309a15a7ade2fc93d271cbaf7142d020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, this also works for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, where no such tilings are possible).\n</p><p><br />\nCase 4: After 2-tiles are placed on each pair of corner-adjacent spaces, the array is reduced to 3 lines each of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cc722503ab9361e9471f3344eef06e4e2bfc7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. This gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef01a58e2a0add927b73f02c37499ab2e707145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{n-3}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"40\" height=\"23\" /> tilings.\n</p><p><br />\nAltogether, the number of tilings is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cc8205a70653bcdb9cdfd85d2034b33a408520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{3n-3} + 2F_{3n-4} + 3F_{3n-5} + 3F_{n-3}F_{2n-4} + F_{n-3}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"371\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO\" title=\"2013 UMO\">2013 UMO </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 UMO Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.utmath.org/home\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 UMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Utah_Math_Olympiad\" title=\"Utah Math Olympiad\"> All UMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232931\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 224/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 905/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9799/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.012      1 Template:UMO_box\n100.00%    7.012      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13439:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232931 and revision id 283770. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}